<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian sugar crush - week to Aug 2.</title>
<headline>Australian sugar crush - week to Aug 2.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's sugar cane crush totalled 1,840,090 tonnes in the week ended August 2, bringing the crush so far this season to 10.69 million tonnes, grower organisation CANEGROWERS said.</p>
<p>This was lower than the 11.20 million tonnes crushed at the same time last year. CANEGROWERS reported for crushing week nine of the 1997 season that average commercial cane sugar (ccs) content was 13.56 percent.</p>
<p>The figures do not include cane crushed in the Ord River region of Western Australia.  </p>
<p>Australian sugar cane crush by region for the week ended August 2 as reported by CANEGROWERS in tonnes.</p>
